      authors: US Bureau of Labor Statistics
      year: 2026
      finding: Of 569,387 private establishments opened in the year to March 1994, 79.6% survived one year, 49.6% five years, 33.6% ten years and 20.3% twenty years. Survivors employed 4.13 million at birth, 3.02 million (73%) after ten years; average employment of survivors rose from 7.2 to 15.8.
      url: https://www.bls.gov/bdm/us_age_naics_00_table7.txt

